Download this repo
1) mkdir workdir
2) cd workdir
3) git clone https://github.com/tuyenhvc/buildroot.git -b develop


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Override kernel source
1) cd workdir
2) git clone https://github.com/tuyenhvc/linux-buildroot-rpi4.git linux -b develop
3) touch buildroot/local.mk and add the below line
LINUX_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$(TOPDIR)/../linux


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Add U-Boot to the boot process
1) cd workdir
2) git clone https://github.com/tuyenhvc/u-boot-buildroot-rpi4.git u-boot -b develop
3) vi buildroot/local.mk to add the below line
UBOOT_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR = UBOOT_OVERRIDE_SRCDIR=$(TOPDIR)/../u-boot


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Step build for pi4
1) make raspberrypi4_64_defconfig
2) make
    => find the kernel, bootloader, root filesystem, sdcard.img etc. in output/images
3) make linux-dirclean (if need to cleanup kernel)
4) make linux-rebuild  (if need to rebuild kernel)
    if terminal show: >>> linux custom Syncing from source dir /your/path/to/kernel , ok linux have beed override
5) make uboot-dirclean (if need to cleanup uboot)


---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Command to flash into sdcard
1) lsblk to check which is your sdcard. VD: sdb
2) sudo umount /dev/sdb*
3) sudo dd if=output/images/sdcard.img of=/dev/sdb bs=4M status=progress conv=fsync
